.\" Manual page for pfadi-default.
.Dd August 7, 2026
.Dt PFADI-DEFAULT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pfadi-default
.Nd use pfadi in place of Finder, as far as macOS allows
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm status | Cm apply | Cm undo
.Nm
.Op Fl h | Fl -help | Fl v | Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
puts
.Xr pfadi 1
where Finder is, and says exactly where that stops.
Every claim it makes about what the system will accept comes from having just
asked it, rather than from an assumption made when it was written.
.Pp
There are four mechanisms, and they are listed separately because they fail
separately.
.Bl -enum
.It
.Em The file viewer .
The global user default
.Va NSFileViewer
decides what
.Dq Finder
means to AppKit.
.Sy selectFile:inFileViewerRootedAtPath:\&
\(em the call behind
.Dq Reveal in Finder ,
.Dq Show in Finder
and
.Dq Show in Enclosing Folder
in other applications \(em reads it, and hands the file to that application
instead of to Finder.
This is the part that genuinely replaces Finder, and it is worth more than the
rest put together.
.It
.Em The shell function .
An
.Ic open
function is written into
.Pa ~/.zshrc
(or
.Pa ~/.bash_profile ) ,
so that
.Ic open .\&
and
.Ic open Ar folder
go to pfadi.
One argument that is a folder goes to pfadi; everything else is handed to the
real
.Xr open 1 ,
so
.Ic open report.pdf
and
.Ic open -a Safari
are unaffected.
.It
.Em The launcher .
A small bundle in
.Pa ~/Applications
so that Spotlight can find pfadi.
It holds the command rather than a copy of the application, so a
.Xr brew 1
upgrade cannot leave it pointing at a version that is no longer installed.
.It
.Em LaunchServices content types .
.Sy public.volume
is handed over.
.Sy public.folder
and
.Sy public.directory
are not: see
.Sx WHAT MACOS REFUSES .
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
What the system has now.
Changes nothing.
This is also what running
.Nm
with no command does.
.It Cm apply
All four mechanisms above.
.It Cm undo
All of it back.
The launcher is removed only when its bundle identifier says pfadi put it there,
and
.Va NSFileViewer
is cleared only when it still names pfadi: an application that is not ours is
somebody's own decision and is left alone.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh WHAT MACOS REFUSES
Double-clicking a folder inside Finder opens Finder, and no setting changes it.
.Pp
.Sy NSWorkspace.setDefaultApplication(at:toOpen:) ,
which is the current interface, answers
.Sy NSCocoaErrorDomain 256
wrapping
.Er paramErr
.Pq -50
for
.Sy public.folder .
The deprecated
.Fn LSSetDefaultRoleHandlerForContentType
answers
.Er paramErr
directly.
The answer does not change with what the application declares in its
.Va CFBundleDocumentTypes ,
nor with the
.Va LSHandlerRank
it declares it at, and
.Xr lsregister 8
.Fl dump
confirms the claim is registered and refused anyway.
The same for the
.Sy file
URL scheme.
Writing the handler into
.Pa ~/Library/Preferences/com.apple.LaunchServices/com.apple.launchservices.secure.plist
directly is accepted and then ignored:
.Nm
does write it, reads back what LaunchServices reports, and says so when the two
disagree.
.Pp
Finder cannot be removed from the Dock either.
It is not in
.Va persistent-apps ;
Dock.app draws it.
Removing it means turning off System Integrity Protection and FileVault and
editing the sealed system volume, which is a bad trade for an icon.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PFADI_APP
The application bundle to point everything at.
Set this when running from a build directory rather than an install.
.It Ev SHELL
Decides which profile the shell function is written to:
.Pa ~/.bash_profile
for a shell whose name ends in
.Sy bash ,
.Pa ~/.zshrc
otherwise.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.zshrc
Holds the
.Ic open
function, between
.Sy "# >>> pfadi instead of finder >>>"
and its closing marker.
.Cm undo
cuts exactly that block out and leaves the rest byte for byte.
.It Pa ~/Applications/Pfadi.app
The launcher.
.It Pa ~/Library/Preferences/.GlobalPreferences.plist
Holds
.Va NSFileViewer .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr defaults 1 ,
.Xr open 1 ,
.Xr pfadi 1
